## 1. DEFINITIONS

In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **"Software"** | The complete program known as Ooraatchi (Web GIS Based Project Management Software), including all source code, object code, compiled binaries, documentation, database schemas, GIS spatial data layers, configuration files, libraries, APIs, mobile applications, user interface designs, and any related material provided by the Licensor. |
| **"Copy"** | Any reproduction, whether full or partial, in any medium (including but not limited to electronic, printed, archived, cloud-hosted, or backup copies). |
| **"Derivative Work"** | Any work that is based upon, incorporates, modifies, translates, adapts, extends, or otherwise changes any portion of the Software. |
| **"Confidential Information"** | Any non-public technical, business, financial, or operational information disclosed by one Party to the other, whether oral, written, or electronic, including but not limited to source code, algorithms, trade secrets, customer data, and pricing information. |
| **"Breach"** | Any act or omission by the Licensee that violates any provision of this Licence Agreement. |
| **"Territory"** | The territory of the Republic of India, unless otherwise agreed in writing by both Parties. |
| **"Effective Date"** | The date on which the Licensee accepts this Licence (by installing, deploying, using, or otherwise accessing the Software), or the date of execution of this Agreement, whichever is earlier. |
| **"GeM"** | Government e-Marketplace (gem.gov.in), the national public procurement platform of the Government of India. |
| **"Work Order"** | The purchase order, contract, or tender award issued by the Licensee (or its parent authority) for procurement of the Software through GeM or any other government procurement channel. |

