## 2. GRANT OF LICENSE

### 2.1 Limited, Non-Exclusive, Non-Transferable Licence
Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, the Licensor hereby grants the Licensee a **limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence** to install, configure, run, and use the Software solely for the Licensee's **internal administrative and governance operations**, including but not limited to:
- Web GIS-based mapping and management of physical infrastructure (electrical poles, water pipelines, municipal buildings) across districts;
- IoT telemetry monitoring for utility assets (overhead water tanks, flow rates, pipeline pressure);
- End-to-end e-tendering, procurement, and work-order lifecycle management;
- Secure vendor management with invite-only quotation access and automated PDF document generation;
- IVR-based automated citizen helpdesk with AI-powered voice processing and ticket creation;
- Field verification and AI-OCR inspection for on-ground quality assurance;
- Multi-tier role-based administration with geo-fenced complaint resolution;
- MIS reporting, analytics dashboards, and automated export of compliance records.

### 2.2 Scope of Use
The licence may be exercised **only** by the Licensee's authorised employees, officers, agents, or contractors who require access to perform the permitted use. The number of users, panchayats, or administrative jurisdictions covered shall be as specified in the Work Order.

### 2.3 No Rights to Source Code
The Licensee receives no right, title, or interest in the source code of the Software, except as expressly provided in Section 3.2.

### 2.4 Installation and Deployment
The Licensee may install and deploy the Software on servers, cloud platforms, or local machines as specified in the Work Order. The Licensor shall provide reasonable technical assistance for initial deployment.

