## 4. RESTRICTIONS

The Licensee shall **NOT**:

1. **Copy, reproduce, distribute, publish, or disclose** the Software (or any part thereof) to any third party, except as expressly permitted in Section 2.
2. **Reverse-engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to derive the source code** of the Software, whether in whole or in part.
3. **Create, distribute, or deploy any Derivative Works** based on the Software.
4. **Sublicense, lease, rent, lend, pledge, or otherwise transfer** the Software or any rights therein to any third party.
5. **Remove, alter, obscure, or deface** any proprietary notices, copyright statements, licence headers, or trademark information embedded in the Software.
6. **Use the Software for any purpose** other than the internal administrative use set out in Section 2.1 — including, without limitation, offering the Software as a hosted service (SaaS), reselling it, or using it for commercial gain outside the scope of the Work Order.
7. **Bypass, disable, or circumvent** any licensing controls, security mechanisms, authentication systems, or API rate limiters embedded in the Software.
8. **Use the Software in any manner that violates applicable law**, including but not limited to data-protection, telecommunications, export-control, and public-procurement regulations.
9. **Benchmark, publicly review, or publish performance metrics** of the Software without the prior written consent of the Licensor.

Any breach of the above restrictions shall constitute a **material breach** of this Agreement and shall trigger the termination provisions set out in Section 8.

